                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "364a0dc2-2ab1-36d7-b8f2-c54d70b4f2ad",
                        "entry_id": "d7d94408-d17a-3a95-85a1-1abaa1d68db8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To take place or occur."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "intransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3059aa8d-f511-44f9-b72a-2cff9fc553de",
                                "sense_id": "364a0dc2-2ab1-36d7-b8f2-c54d70b4f2ad",
                                "text": "True, there might be a slight difficulty in the shame, but as regarded the sin, there was no item of that kind ever scored down on the Bar-slate that had its own familiar peg whereon to hang such tales of evil as must pain and shock every pure mind—tales of devilish import, eventualizing, in most instances, most grievously and banefully—in rags, want of food, perhaps in crime, and almost, for certain, in pauperism!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ed92fcc5-f363-496b-9de7-732421461285",
                                "sense_id": "364a0dc2-2ab1-36d7-b8f2-c54d70b4f2ad",
                                "text": "In thus intuscepting the fundamental and initiative momenta of itself, the Self cognizes the exercise of three classes of powers which eventualize as forces, and which are still further analyzable into three simple discrete elementary powers."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "46de9efd-a60d-488f-9985-88a546a282d4",
                                "sense_id": "364a0dc2-2ab1-36d7-b8f2-c54d70b4f2ad",
                                "text": "Doctors are not accustomed to dwell pessimistically on the future problems of their patients. If the problem does eventualize, it can be handled then."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
